.SH NAME
CWE\-84 \- Improper Neutralization of Encoded URI Schemes in a Web Page
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The web application improperly neutralizes user\-controlled input for executable script disguised with URI encodings.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB1\fR exploited CVE mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2026\-96654
Plex Media Server, added 2026\-10\-20.
.PP
Plex Media Server Improper Neutralization of Encoded URI Schemes in a Web Page Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Plex Media Server contains an improper neutralization of encoded URI schemes in a web page vulnerability that could allow an attacker to call other plugins' functions and supply their own parameters. This vulnerability can be chained with CVE\-2026\-96652, CVE\-2026\-96655, and CVE\-2026\-96656.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply vendor mitigations; follow CISA BOD 26\-04 (risk\-based patching) and forensics triage. Discontinue use if no mitigation exists.
 Due 2026\-10\-23.
.PP
